01:33:44,859 --> 01:33:50,412
So, you know, there are opportunities and good things about it, even though it's

1131
01:33:53,465 --> 01:33:54,286
not ideal.

1132
01:33:55,326 --> 01:34:14,380
So I think it's important to always take it with a grain of salt, always recognize that it's not a panacea or perfect, but it is better than current practice, I guess.

1133
01:34:17,904 --> 01:34:20,366
Well, I guess we'll see in 20 years.

1134
01:34:21,466 --> 01:34:24,909
Well, yeah.

1135
01:34:25,189 --> 01:34:28,831
It needs to be an iterative process.

1136
01:34:29,132 --> 01:34:31,113
As of today, yes, it's better.

1137
01:34:31,353 --> 01:34:35,076
As of five years from now, maybe it's not better.

1138
01:34:35,396 --> 01:34:39,439
So it needs to keep evolving.

1139
01:34:39,459 --> 01:34:42,100
I agree.

1140
01:34:42,561 --> 01:34:43,662
We can't switch right away.

1141
01:34:44,582 --> 01:34:45,022
We need to.

1142
01:34:46,696 --> 01:34:55,340
I was gonna say one of the issues is there will be a push to convert to electric means for the heat pumps and whatnot.

1143
01:34:56,981 --> 01:35:12,188
There will still be those how homes that will not convert and they will, but you would hope that the demand for natural gas overall or methane will be reduced.

1144
